{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>The El of Beth El.</b> Like 'El of Beth El' — the heh is superfluous, and the manner of Scripture is to speak thus, as in ״כִּי אַתֶּם בָאִים אֶל הָאָרֶץ כְּנַעַן״ (Numbers 34)." "<b>You anointed there.</b> A term of greatness and grandeur — as one is anointed for kingship, so ״וַיִּצֹק שֶׁמֶן עַל רֹאשָׁהּ״ — to be anointed for the altar." "<b>Which you vowed to Me.</b> And you must fulfill it — for you said, 'It shall be a house of Elohim,' that you would offer sacrifices there."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:01:31.796107943Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}